meta {
  name: Gated site — is the browser session working?
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/connectors/{{scrapeConnector}}/browser/session
}

docs {
  For a `web_scrape` connector with `use_browser=true` (a site behind a login).

  Fetches the connector's start URL **through the saved browser session** and reports
  whether it got content or a sign-in page. A saved profile alone proves nothing — this
  is what distinguishes "signed in" from "silently ingesting zero documents", because a
  gated site answers an unauthenticated request with `200 OK` and a login form rather
  than an error.

  `?verify=false` skips the live fetch and answers from stored cookies alone — cheap
  enough to poll while a sign-in window is open.

  `remote_capable` says whether this host would run a NEW sign-in as a remote
  (screencast) session rather than a local window — independent of whether one is
  currently running, so a UI can decide up front which flow "Sign in" opens. The
  in-flight `login` object (when present) carries `mode: "local" | "remote"` for the
  same reason once a sign-in is actually running.
}
